$homeMain = @"
<section class="home-hero">
  <img class="home-hero-image" src="$BasePath/assets/axentra-operations-visual.jpg" alt="Legal and business process teams reviewing documents and workflow information" width="1774" height="887" fetchpriority="high" />
  <div class="home-hero-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="container home-hero-content">
    <p class="eyebrow">Alternative legal and business process services</p>
    <h1>An extended specialist team for legal and business processes</h1>
    <div class="home-hero-copy">
      <p>Axentra works alongside law firms, in-house teams, lenders, servicers and legal, contract and property technology companies in India and international markets.</p>
      <p>We take responsibility for defined projects, on-demand requirements, recurring managed workflows and secondments. Teams are structured around the work, required experience, client systems, time zones, review layers and reporting expectations.</p>
      <p>Technology and AI are used where they improve speed, consistency or visibility. Trained professionals remain responsible for review, judgement, exceptions and quality.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="$BasePath/services/">Explore Services</a><a class="button secondary" href="$BasePath/contact.html">Discuss Your Requirement</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="hero-facts-band" aria-label="Engagement and delivery options"><div class="container hero-facts-grid"><div><p>Ways to engage</p><ul class="engagement-strip"><li>On-demand requirements</li><li>Defined projects</li><li>Managed workflows</li><li>Dedicated teams</li><li>Secondments</li></ul></div><div><p>Delivery coverage</p><ul class="delivery-strip"><li>India-based delivery</li><li>India and international clients</li><li>Time-zone-aligned teams</li><li>Planned holiday and peak-volume coverage</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="section extension-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Extended specialist team</p><h2>Working as an extension of your team</h2></div><div><p>Axentra takes on a defined part of the client's legal or business process, with agreed responsibilities, review points, reporting and escalation routes.</p><p>The team works within the client's systems or other approved environments and remains aligned with the client's instructions, working hours and service expectations.</p><p>Depending on the requirement, Axentra delivers through a dedicated team, a managed workflow, project-based capacity, on-demand resources or professionals seconded into the client's team.</p></div></div><div class="principle-grid"><article><h3>Integrated with the client environment</h3><p>Work is performed within the systems, instructions, templates and communication channels agreed for the engagement.</p></article><article><h3>Responsible for the agreed delivery</h3><p>Roles, outputs, quality checks, deadlines, dependencies and escalation routes are defined before work begins.</p></article><article><h3>Flexible team structure</h3><p>Team size, roles, seniority, review levels and working hours reflect the particular engagement.</p></article><article><h3>Visible delivery</h3><p>Clients receive agreed reporting on completed work, open items, dependencies, quality findings and matters requiring attention.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-muted home-services"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Primary services</p><h2>Five specialist service areas</h2></div><p>Each service page explains the activities, boundaries and information needed to begin.</p></div>$serviceCards</div></section>
<section class="section section-dark quality-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Quality assurance</p><h2>Quality is part of the delivery</h2></div><div><p>Quality is not treated only as a final check.</p><p>Each engagement defines how work is prepared, reviewed, approved, escalated and reported. The review structure reflects the nature of the work, the level of risk, client requirements and the experience of the assigned team.</p></div></div><div class="quality-grid"><article><h3>Clear quality criteria</h3><p>Instructions, templates, checklists, expected outputs and escalation points are agreed and calibrated at the beginning of delivery.</p></article><article><h3>Review layers</h3><p>Production checks, supervisory review, sampling or independent QA are arranged according to the engagement and client requirements.</p></article><article><h3>Exceptions recorded and resolved</h3><p>Missing information, inconsistencies, unusual cases and unclear instructions are recorded, routed and tracked rather than resolved informally.</p></article><article><h3>Findings used to improve delivery</h3><p>Recurring findings help identify issues in intake, instructions, templates, training, systems, allocation, review or escalation.</p></article></div><div class="quality-arrangements"><div><p class="eyebrow">Engagement-specific QA</p><h3>Quality arrangements can include</h3><p>The review and QA structure is agreed according to the project or managed workflow.</p></div>$(Get-ListMarkup -Items @('Initial sample validation','Calibration exercises','First-line checks','Supervisory review','Independent QA','Risk-based sampling','Exception registers','Rework tracking','Root-cause analysis','Corrective action','Trend reporting','Client feedback','Refresher training','Updates to instructions and checklists') -ClassName 'output-list quality-list')</div></div></section>
<section class="section technology-section"><div class="container detail-layout"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Technology and accountability</p><h2>Comfortable with technology. Accountable for the output.</h2><p>Axentra works within client and approved platforms and uses technology, automation and AI where they improve delivery, consistency or visibility.</p><p>Technology does not remove accountability for the output.</p><p>Trained professionals review the work against source documents, client instructions, templates, playbooks and agreed quality criteria. Human judgement remains central where context, commercial meaning, legal language, exceptions or unclear information require review.</p></div><div><h3>Technology can assist with</h3>$(Get-ListMarkup -Items @('Document classification','Data extraction','Clause comparison','Draft preparation','Workflow routing','Tracking','Validation','Reporting','Identifying exceptions','Reviewing larger document sets') -ClassName 'output-list')<p class="boundary-note">Client information is not entered into unauthorised public AI tools or used for independent model training.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section section-muted value-section"><div class="container detail-layout"><div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Delivery insight</p><h2>More than task completion</h2><p>During delivery, Axentra records recurring errors, avoidable rework, missing information, unclear instructions, process delays and other patterns affecting quality or turnaround.</p><p>Where a pattern is relevant to the agreed scope, Axentra shares findings and improvement options with the client.</p><p>The purpose is to make useful delivery findings visible and help the client decide where improvement is worthwhile.</p></div><div><h3>Recommendations can relate to</h3>$(Get-ListMarkup -Items @('Intake forms','Data requirements','Templates','Playbooks','SOPs','Review checklists','Training','Work allocation','Handoffs','Escalation routes','Reporting','Quality sampling','Product logic','AI prompts','Extraction instructions','Test cases','User guidance') -ClassName 'output-list')<p class="boundary-note">Changes to the client's process, product, instructions or systems are introduced only after client review and agreement.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section engagement-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Engagement models</p><h2>Ways to work with Axentra</h2></div><p>The delivery arrangement follows the scope, volumes, duration, required experience, systems, review requirements and client working hours.</p></div><div class="engagement-grid"><article><h3>On-demand requirements</h3><p>Specialist capacity for short-term needs, deadlines, backlogs, workload peaks, leave coverage or temporary resource gaps.</p></article><article><h3>Defined projects</h3><p>A team and delivery plan arranged around a specific scope, timeline, output and completion criteria.</p></article><article><h3>Managed workflows</h3><p>Ongoing delivery for recurring business needs, with agreed instructions, quality checks, reporting and escalation.</p></article><article><h3>Dedicated teams</h3><p>Teams arranged around the client's volumes, required roles, systems, working hours and review structure.</p></article><article><h3>Secondments</h3><p>Professionals assigned for an agreed period to work within the client's team, systems, reporting lines and working hours.</p></article></div><p class="engagement-note">Working hours, time-zone overlap, holiday coverage and extended-hour requirements are agreed through the staffing and delivery plan.</p></div></section>
<section class="section section-dark assessment-cta"><div class="container compact-split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Workflow Assessment</p><h2>Define the work before proposing the team</h2><p>Axentra reviews volumes, systems, skills, review responsibilities, working hours and transition needs before proposing a delivery structure.</p></div><a class="button secondary" href="$BasePath/services/workflow-assessment.html">Explore Workflow Assessment</a></div></section>
"@

